  "output": "## Test Coverage Analysis\n\n**Tested:** `routes.ts`, `validation.ts`\n**Untested:** everything else shown — `api.ts`, `utils/config.ts`, `utils/errors.ts`, `utils/formatting.ts`, `utils/transcript.ts`, `utils/cache.ts`, `hooks/useCountUp.ts`, `hooks/useToasts.ts`, `hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts`\n\n---\n\n### 1. `src/api.ts` — highest risk, zero coverage\n\nUntested: `getToken`/`setToken`/`clearToken`, `apiUrl`, `request()` (auth header injection, 401 auto-clear, non-2xx → `ApiError`, 204 handling, JSON parse).\n\n**Gaps:**\n- 401 response should clear token but current code doesn't `throw` before also hitting the `!response.ok` branch — worth a test to pin behavior (does caller get `ApiError(401, ...)` after clear, or silently get `undefined`?).\n- `apiUrl` with absolute URL vs relative, leading-slash normalization.\n- `request` when body text-read itself fails (`.catch(() => '')`).\n\n```ts\n// src/api.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, beforeEach, vi } from 'vitest';\nimport { getToken, setToken, clearToken, apiUrl, ApiError } from './api';\n\ndescribe('token storage', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => localStorage.clear());\n\n  it('returns empty string when no token set', () => {\n    expect(getToken()).toBe('');\n  });\n  it('round-trips a token', () => {\n    setToken('abc');\n    expect(getToken()).toBe('abc');\n  });\n  it('clearToken removes it', () => {\n    setToken('abc');\n    clearToken();\n    expect(getToken()).toBe('');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('apiUrl', () => {\n  it('passes through absolute http(s) urls unchanged', () => {\n    expect(apiUrl('https://foo.com/x')).toBe('https://foo.com/x');\n  });\n  it('prefixes relative paths with API_BASE, normalizing missing leading slash', () => {\n    expect(apiUrl('bots')).toMatch(/\\/bots$/);\n    expect(apiUrl('/bots')).toMatch(/\\/bots$/);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('request() via fetch mock', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => {\n    localStorage.clear();\n    vi.restoreAllMocks();\n  });\n\n  it('attaches Authorization header when a token is present', async () => {\n    setToken('tok123');\n    const fetchSpy = vi.spyOn(global, 'fetch').mockResolvedValue(\n      new Response(JSON.stringify({ ok: true }), { status: 200 })\n    );\n    // exercise a real exported call that hits request(), e.g. listBots()/getBot()\n    // await listBots();\n    expect(fetchSpy).toHaveBeenCalledWith(\n      expect.any(String),\n      expect.objectContaining({ headers: expect.objectContaining({ Authorization: 'Bearer tok123' }) })\n    );\n  });\n\n  it('clears token on 401 response', async () => {\n    setToken('stale');\n    vi.spyOn(global, 'fetch').mockResolvedValue(new Response('', { status: 401 }));\n    await expect(/* some api call */ Promise.resolve()).rejects; // replace with real call\n    expect(getToken()).toBe('');\n  });\n\n  it('throws ApiError with status + body text on non-ok response', async () => {\n    vi.spyOn(global, 'fetch').mockResolvedValue(new Response('bad request', { status: 400 }));\n    await expect(/* api call */ Promise.reject(new ApiError(400, 'bad request'))).rejects.toBeInstanceOf(ApiError);\n  });\n\n  it('returns undefined for 204 No Content without parsing body', async () => {\n    vi.spyOn(global, 'fetch').mockResolvedValue(new Response(null, { status: 204 }));\n    // const result = await deleteBot('id');\n    // expect(result).toBeUndefined();\n  });\n\n  it('falls back to statusText when error body text read fails', async () => {\n    const res = new Response('', { status: 500, statusText: 'Server Error' });\n    vi.spyOn(res, 'text').mockRejectedValue(new Error('stream closed'));\n    vi.spyOn(global, 'fetch').mockResolvedValue(res);\n    // expect thrown ApiError.message to be 'Server Error'\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `src/utils/errors.ts` — branch-heavy, untested\n\n**Gaps:** every branch of `classifyNetworkError` (timeout/api, timeout/test, failed-to-fetch/api, failed-to-fetch/test), each LiveKit-specific string in `friendlyTestError`, `summarizeDetails` truncation to 4 entries, `average([])` empty-array edge case, `buildDiagnostic` message truncation at 220 chars.\n\n```ts\n// src/utils/errors.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';\nimport { friendlyApiError, friendlyTestError, summarizeDetails, average, buildDiagnostic } from './errors';\n\ndescribe('friendlyApiError', () => {\n  it('adds context for \"network timeout\"', () => {\n    expect(friendlyApiError(new Error('network timeout'))).toContain('Mongo/LiveKit');\n  });\n  it('adds context for \"failed to fetch\"', () => {\n    expect(friendlyApiError(new Error('failed to fetch'))).toContain('start_api.sh');\n  });\n  it('passes through unrecognized errors verbatim', () => {\n    expect(friendlyApiError(new Error('boom'))).toBe('boom');\n  });\n  it('stringifies non-Error values', () => {\n    expect(friendlyApiError('plain string')).toBe('plain string');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('friendlyTestError', () => {\n  it('flags unconfigured LiveKit', () => {\n    expect(friendlyTestError(new Error('LiveKit is not configured'))).toMatch(/LIVEKIT_URL/);\n  });\n  it('flags room-creation failure', () => {\n    expect(friendlyTestError(new Error('Could not create LiveKit test room'))).toMatch(/credentials/);\n  });\n  it('flags microphone permission errors case-insensitively', () => {\n    expect(friendlyTestError(new Error('Permission denied for MICROPHONE'))).toMatch(/microphone/i);\n  });\n  it('flags websocket/network errors', () => {\n    expect(friendlyTestError(new Error('WebSocket connection failed'))).toMatch(/ws\\/wss/);\n  });\n  it('falls back to generic message for unknown errors', () => {\n    expect(friendlyTestError(new Error(''))).toBe('Unknown test call error. Check backend logs and LiveKit server status.');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('summarizeDetails', () => {\n  it('caps output at 4 entries', () => {\n    const details = { a: 1, b: 2, c: 3, d: 4, e: 5 };\n    expect(summarizeDetails(details).split(' | ')).toHaveLength(4);\n  });\n  it('JSON-stringifies object values, stringifies primitives', () => {\n    expect(summarizeDetails({ x: { nested: 1 } })).toContain('{\"nested\":1}');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('average', () => {\n  it('returns 0 for empty array', () => {\n    expect(average([])).toBe(0);\n  });\n  it('rounds the mean', () => {\n    expect(average([1, 2])).toBe(2); // rounds 1.5 -> 2 (banker's? verify Math.round behavior)\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('buildDiagnostic', () => {\n  it('truncates messages over 220 chars with ellipsis', () => {\n    const long = new Error('x'.repeat(300));\n    const d = buildDiagnostic('scope', long);\n    expect(d.message.endsWith('...')).toBe(true);\n    expect(d.message.length).toBeLessThanOrEqual(223);\n  });\n  it('defaults severity to error', () => {\n    expect(buildDiagnostic('scope', new Error('e')).severity).toBe('error');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. `src/utils/formatting.ts` — date/timezone edge cases untested\n\n**Gaps:** `parseApiDate` timezone-suffix detection (`Z`, `+05:30`, no suffix), invalid date fallback to raw string in `formatDate`/`formatTime`, `timeAgo` boundary values (59s/60s, 3599s/3600s, 86399s/86400s, 172799s/172800s), `titleCase` with empty/undefined and multi-delimiter input.\n\n```ts\n// src/utils/formatting.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';\nimport { shortId, parseApiDate, formatDate, timeAgo, titleCase } from './formatting';\n\ndescribe('shortId', () => {\n  it('returns \"-\" for empty string', () => expect(shortId('')).toBe('-'));\n  it('leaves short ids untouched', () => expect(shortId('abc123')).toBe('abc123'));\n  it('truncates long ids with ellipsis', () => expect(shortId('abcdefghijklmnop')).toBe('abcdefgh...mnop'));\n});\n\ndescribe('parseApiDate', () => {\n  it('treats a string without timezone as UTC by appending Z', () => {\n    const d = parseApiDate('2026-01-01T00:00:00');\n    expect(d.toISOString()).toBe('2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z');\n  });\n  it('leaves an explicit Z suffix untouched', () => {\n    expect(parseApiDate('2026-01-01T00:00:00Z').toISOString()).toBe('2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z');\n  });\n  it('leaves an explicit offset untouched', () => {\n    expect(parseApiDate('2026-01-01T00:00:00+05:30').getUTCHours()).toBe(18); // prev day 18:30 UTC\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('formatDate', () => {\n  it('returns \"-\" for missing value', () => expect(formatDate(undefined)).toBe('-'));\n  it('returns raw value for unparseable date', () => expect(formatDate('not-a-date')).toBe('not-a-date'));\n});\n\ndescribe('timeAgo', () => {\n  it('returns \"-\" for missing value', () => expect(timeAgo(undefined)).toBe('-'));\n  beforeEachBoundaryCases();\n  function beforeEachBoundaryCases() {\n    it.each([\n      [30, 'just now'],\n      [90, '1 min ago'],\n      [3700, '1 hr ago'],\n    ])('classifies %i seconds ago correctly', (secs, expected) => {\n      vi.setSystemTime(Date.now());\n      const iso = new Date(Date.now() - secs * 1000).toISOString();\n      expect(timeAgo(iso)).toBe(expected);\n    });\n  }\n  it('returns \"yesterday\" for 1-2 day range', () => {\n    const iso = new Date(Date.now() - 90000 * 1000).toISOString();\n    expect(timeAgo(iso)).toBe('yesterday');\n  });\n  it('falls back to formatDate beyond 2 days', () => {\n    const iso = new Date(Date.now() - 3 * 86400 * 1000).toISOString();\n    expect(timeAgo(iso)).toBe(formatDate(iso));\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('titleCase', () => {\n  it('returns \"-\" for empty/undefined', () => expect(titleCase(undefined)).toBe('-'));\n  it('splits on underscores, hyphens, and spaces', () => {\n    expect(titleCase('short_hangup-not interested')).toBe('Short Hangup Not Interested');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 4. `src/utils/transcript.ts` — most complex logic, zero coverage, high regression risk (adjacent to the recent JIRA-AI-148 change)\n\n**Gaps:**\n- `buildConversationItems` with no transcript → `[]`.\n- Selection precedence: `verified_transcript` (only when status `'succeeded'` AND non-empty) vs `transcript` vs `live_transcript` fallback chain.\n- Branch split on `hasTurnTimes`: merged+sorted path vs bucketed start/middle/end path.\n- `normalizeTranscriptRole` covering every alias bucket and the unknown-role fallback.\n- `timestampValue` with missing/invalid date → `MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` (sorts last).\n- `transcriptSourceLabel` covering all four `verified_transcript_status` branches plus the default fallback.\n- `maxResponseDelayLabel` threshold boundaries (2999/3000, 7999/8000) and the \"no delay\" `'-'` case.\n\n```ts\n// src/utils/transcript.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';\nimport {\n  buildConversationItems, normalizeTranscriptRole, timestampValue,\n  transcriptSourceLabel, maxResponseDelayLabel\n} from './transcript';\nimport type { Transcript, CallEvent } from '../api';\n\ndescribe('buildConversationItems', () => {\n  it('returns empty array when transcript is undefined', () => {\n    expect(buildConversationItems(undefined, [])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it('prefers verified_transcript only when status succeeded and non-empty', () => {\n    const t = {\n      transcript: [{ role: 'user', text: 'raw' }],\n      verified_transcript: [{ role: 'user', text: 'verified' }],\n      verified_transcript_status: 'succeeded',\n    } as unknown as Transcript;\n    const items = buildConversationItems(t, []);\n    expect(items.some((i) => i.kind === 'turn' && i.text === 'verified')).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it('falls back to transcript when verified status is pending', () => {\n    const t = {\n      transcript: [{ role: 'user', text: 'raw' }],\n      verified_transcript: [{ role: 'user', text: 'verified' }],\n      verified_transcript_status: 'pending',\n    } as unknown as Transcript;\n    const items = buildConversationItems(t, []);\n    expect(items.some((i) => i.kind === 'turn' && i.text === 'raw')).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it('falls back to live_transcript when transcript is absent', () => {\n    const t = { live_transcript: [{ role: 'assistant', text: 'live' }] } as unknown as Transcript;\n    expect(buildConversationItems(t, []).some((i) => i.kind === 'turn' && i.text === 'live')).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  it('interleaves and sorts by time when turns carry created_at', () => {\n    const t = {\n      transcript: [\n        { role: 'user', text: 'b', created_at: '2026-01-01T00:00:02Z' },\n        { role: 'user', text: 'a', created_at: '2026-01-01T00:00:01Z' },\n      ],\n    } as unknown as Transcript;\n    const items = buildConversationItems(t, []);\n    expect(items.map((i) => (i as any).text)).toEqual(['a', 'b']);\n  });\n\n  it('buckets events into start/middle/end when turns lack created_at', () => {\n    const t = { transcript: [{ role: 'user', text: 'x' }] } as unknown as Transcript;\n    const events: CallEvent[] = [\n      { _id: '1', event_type: 'call_started', created_at: '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z' },\n      { _id: '2', event_type: 'call_ended', created_at: '2026-01-01T00:00:05Z' },\n    ];\n    const items = buildConversationItems(t, events);\n    expect(items[0]).toMatchObject({ kind: 'event', title: 'call_started' });\n    expect(items[items.length - 1]).toMatchObject({ kind: 'event', title: 'call_ended' });\n  });\n\n  it('filters out events not in INLINE_EVENT_TYPES', () => {\n    const t = { transcript: [] } as unknown as Transcript;\n    const events: CallEvent[] = [{ _id: '1', event_type: 'unrelated_event', created_at: '2026-01-01T00:00:00Z' }];\n    expect(buildConversationItems(t, events)).toEqual([]);\n  });\n\n  it('marks turn interrupted from interrupted flag or event_type substring', () => {\n    const t = {\n      transcript: [{ role: 'user', text: 'x', event_type: 'user_interruption' }],\n    } as unknown as Transcript;\n    const items = buildConversationItems(t, []);\n    expect((items[0] as any).interrupted).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('normalizeTranscriptRole', () => {\n  it.each([\n    ['assistant', 'assistant'], ['agent', 'assistant'], ['bot', 'assistant'], ['model', 'assistant'],\n    ['user', 'user'], ['customer', 'user'], ['caller', 'user'], ['human', 'user'],\n    ['recording', 'recording'], ['verified_recording', 'recording'],\n    ['unknown_role', 'unknown_role'],\n    ['', 'system'],\n  ])('maps %s -> %s', (input, expected) => {\n    expect(normalizeTranscriptRole(input)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('timestampValue', () => {\n  it('returns MAX_SAFE_INTEGER for missing value', () => {\n    expect(timestampValue(undefined)).toBe(Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER);\n  });\n  it('returns MAX_SAFE_INTEGER for unparseable value', () => {\n    expect(timestampValue('not-a-date')).toBe(Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER);\n  });\n  it('returns epoch ms for valid iso string', () => {\n    expect(timestampValue('2026-01-01T00:00:00Z')).toBe(Date.parse('2026-01-01T00:00:00Z'));\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('transcriptSourceLabel', () => {\n  it.each([\n    ['succeeded', 'Verified recording'],\n    ['pending', 'Live transcript, verification pending'],\n    ['failed', 'Live transcript, verification failed'],\n    ['unavailable', 'Live transcript, recording unavailable'],\n  ])('status %s -> %s', (status, expected) => {\n    expect(transcriptSourceLabel({ verified_transcript_status: status } as any)).toBe(expected);\n  });\n  it('falls back to analysis_transcript_source/transcript_source/\"gemini live\"', () => {\n    expect(transcriptSourceLabel({} as any)).toBe('Gemini Live');\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('maxResponseDelayLabel', () => {\n  it('returns \"-\" when no latency metrics', () => {\n    expect(maxResponseDelayLabel({} as any)).toBe('-');\n  });\n  it('labels below 3000ms plain', () => {\n    expect(maxResponseDelayLabel({ latency_metrics: { max_response_delay_ms: 2999 } } as any)).toBe('2999ms');\n  });\n  it('labels 3000-7999ms as slow', () => {\n    expect(maxResponseDelayLabel({ latency_metrics: { max_response_delay_ms: 3000 } } as any)).toBe('3000ms slow');\n  });\n  it('labels >=8000ms as high', () => {\n    expect(maxResponseDelayLabel({ latency_metrics: { max_response_delay_ms: 8000 } } as any)).toBe('8000ms high');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 5. `src/utils/config.ts` — parse/derive logic untested\n\n```ts\n// src/utils/config.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';\nimport { parseConfig, deriveAgentState } from './config';\n\ndescribe('parseConfig', () => {\n  it('returns ok:true with parsed value for valid JSON', () => {\n    expect(parseConfig('{\"a\":1}')).toEqual({ ok: true, value: { a: 1 } });\n  });\n  it('returns ok:false with error message for invalid JSON', () => {\n    const result = parseConfig('{not json');\n    expect(result.ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('deriveAgentState', () => {\n  it('returns idle when hasRoom is false regardless of status', () => {\n    expect(deriveAgentState('speaking', false, false)).toBe('idle');\n  });\n  it('returns idle for disconnected status', () => {\n    expect(deriveAgentState('Disconnected', false, true)).toBe('idle');\n  });\n  it('returns connecting for connecting/creating/requesting/reconnecting substrings', () => {\n    expect(deriveAgentState('Creating room', false, true)).toBe('connecting');\n    expect(deriveAgentState('Reconnecting...', false, true)).toBe('connecting');\n  });\n  it('returns speaking when remoteAudioReady is true even if status is neutral', () => {\n    expect(deriveAgentState('room joined', true, true)).toBe('speaking');\n  });\n  it('returns thinking for \"waiting for bot\"/\"participant joined\"', () => {\n    expect(deriveAgentState('Participant joined', false, true)).toBe('thinking');\n  });\n  it('defaults to listening otherwise', () => {\n    expect(deriveAgentState('Connected', false, true)).toBe('listening');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 6. `src/utils/cache.ts` — silent-failure paths untested\n\n**Gaps:** `cacheSet`/`cacheGet` happy path, `cacheGet` returning fallback on missing key or malformed JSON, `cacheSet` swallowing quota-exceeded errors, `pruneOldCache` removing stale-prefix keys but keeping current-prefix keys.\n\n```ts\n// src/utils/cache.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi, beforeEach } from 'vitest';\nimport { cacheSet, cacheGet, pruneOldCache, CACHE_PREFIX } from './cache';\n\ndescribe('cacheSet/cacheGet', () => {\n  beforeEach(() => localStorage.clear());\n\n  it('round-trips a JSON-serializable value', () => {\n    cacheSet('key', { a: 1 });\n    expect(cacheGet('key', null)).toEqual({ a: 1 });\n  });\n  it('returns fallback when key is missing', () => {\n    expect(cacheGet('missing', 'fallback')).toBe('fallback');\n  });\n  it('returns fallback when stored value is malformed JSON', () => {\n    localStorage.setItem(`${CACHE_PREFIX}bad`, '{not json');\n    expect(cacheGet('bad', 'fallback')).toBe('fallback');\n  });\n  it('swallows storage errors on set (e.g. quota exceeded)', () => {\n    vi.spyOn(Storage.prototype, 'setItem').mockImplementation(() => { throw new Error('quota'); });\n    expect(() => cacheSet('key', 'value')).not.toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe('pruneOldCache', () => {\n  it('removes keys with the old jd-vb: prefix but not the current version', () => {\n    localStorage.setItem('jd-vb:v1:stale', 'x');\n    localStorage.setItem(`${CACHE_PREFIX}fresh`, 'y');\n    pruneOldCache();\n    expect(localStorage.getItem('jd-vb:v1:stale')).toBeNull();\n    expect(localStorage.getItem(`${CACHE_PREFIX}fresh`)).toBe('y');\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 7. `src/hooks/useCountUp.ts` — memory-leak risk, untested\n\n**Gap:** unmounting mid-animation doesn't cancel the in-flight `requestAnimationFrame`, so `setValue` can fire on an unmounted component (flagged in prior perf audit as a leak). Also `target === 0` reset path.\n\n```ts\n// src/hooks/useCountUp.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';\nimport { renderHook } from '@testing-library/react';\nimport { useCountUp } from './useCountUp';\n\ndescribe('useCountUp', () => {\n  it('resets to 0 immediately when target is 0', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useCountUp(0));\n    expect(result.current.value).toBe(0);\n  });\n\n  it('does not throw or update state after unmount mid-animation', async () => {\n    const { unmount } = renderHook(() => useCountUp(100, 500));\n    unmount();\n    await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 50));\n    // regression test: currently no cancelAnimationFrame on unmount — this\n    // documents the gap noted in the prior perf audit (potential leak).\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 8. `src/hooks/useToasts.ts` — timer cleanup untested\n\n**Gap:** `setTimeout` in `showToast` is untracked; if `dismissToast` is called manually before the timer fires, or the component unmounts, the timer isn't cleared (perf audit flagged this).\n\n```ts\n// src/hooks/useToasts.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';\nimport { renderHook, act } from '@testing-library/react';\nimport { useToasts } from './useToasts';\n\ndescribe('useToasts', () => {\n  it('adds a toast and auto-dismisses after durationMs', () => {\n    vi.useFakeTimers();\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useToasts());\n    act(() => { result.current.showToast('hi'); });\n    expect(result.current.toasts).toHaveLength(1);\n    act(() => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(4000); });\n    expect(result.current.toasts).toHaveLength(0);\n    vi.useRealTimers();\n  });\n\n  it('does not auto-dismiss when durationMs is 0', () => {\n    vi.useFakeTimers();\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useToasts());\n    act(() => { result.current.showToast('persist', 'info', 0); });\n    act(() => { vi.advanceTimersByTime(10000); });\n    expect(result.current.toasts).toHaveLength(1);\n    vi.useRealTimers();\n  });\n\n  it('manual dismissToast before timer fires does not error on later timer callback', () => {\n    vi.useFakeTimers();\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useToasts());\n    let id = '';\n    act(() => { id = result.current.showToast('x'); });\n    act(() => { result.current.dismissToast(id); });\n    expect(() => vi.advanceTimersByTime(5000)).not.toThrow();\n    vi.useRealTimers();\n  });\n\n  it('assigns unique incrementing ids across calls', () => {\n    const { result } = renderHook(() => useToasts());\n    act(() => { result.current.showToast('a'); result.current.showToast('b'); });\n    const ids = result.current.toasts.map((t) => t.id);\n    expect(new Set(ids).size).toBe(2);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### 9. `src/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts` — untested despite non-trivial guard logic\n\n**Gaps:** ignores keys when focus is in `INPUT`/`TEXTAREA`/`SELECT` or `contentEditable`; `Escape` always closes; `?` toggles regardless of modifiers; any modifier key (meta/ctrl/alt) suppresses shortcut matching; unmatched keys are no-ops; listener registered once (refs stay current across re-renders).\n\n```ts\n// src/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.test.tsx\nimport { describe, it, expect, vi } from 'vitest';\nimport { renderHook } from '@testing-library/react';\nimport { useKeyboardShortcuts } from './useKeyboardShortcuts';\n\nfunction fireKey(props: Partial<KeyboardEventInit> & { target?: EventTarget }) {\n  const event = new KeyboardEvent('keydown', { key: props.key, bubbles: true, cancelable: true, ...props });\n  (props.target || window).dispatchEvent(event);\n}\n\ndescribe('useKeyboardShortcuts', () => {\n  it('ignores keystrokes when focus is in an input field', () => {\n    const navigate = vi.fn();\n    renderHook(() => useKeyboardShortcuts(navigate, vi.fn(), vi.fn()));\n    const input = document.createElement('input');\n    document.body.appendChild(input);\n    input.focus();\n    fireKey({ key: 'b', target: input });\n    expect(navigate).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it('closes modal on Escape regardless of focus', () => {\n    const closeModal = vi.fn();\n    renderHook(() => useKeyboardShortcuts(vi.fn(), vi.fn(), closeModal));\n    fireKey({ key: 'Escape' });\n    expect(closeModal).toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it('toggles shortcuts panel on \"?\"', () => {\n    const toggle = vi.fn();\n    renderHook(() => useKeyboardShortcuts(vi.fn(), toggle, vi.fn()));\n    fireKey({ key: '?' });\n    expect(toggle).toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it('ignores shortcut keys when a modifier is held', () => {\n    const navigate = vi.fn();\n    renderHook(() => useKeyboardShortcuts(navigate, vi.fn(), vi.fn()));\n    fireKey({ key: 'b', metaKey: true });\n    expect(navigate).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n\n  it('navigates on a matched shortcut key from SHORTCUT_MAP', () => {\n    const navigate = vi.fn();\n    renderHook(() => useKeyboardShortcuts(navigate, vi.fn(), vi.fn()));\n    // pick a real key from SHORTCUT_MAP, e.g. 'g' -> some view\n    // fireKey({ key: 'g' });\n    // expect(navigate).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expectedView);\n  });\n\n  it('always calls the latest navigate callback after re-render (ref pattern)', () => {\n    const navigate1 = vi.fn();\n    const navigate2 = vi.fn();\n    const { rerender } = renderHook(({ nav }) => useKeyboardShortcuts(nav, vi.fn(), vi.fn()), {\n      initialProps: { nav: navigate1 },\n    });\n    rerender({ nav: navigate2 });\n    // fireKey({ key: 'g' });\n    // expect(navigate2).toHaveBeenCalled();\n    // expect(navigate1).not.toHaveBeenCalled();\n  });\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n### Priority order for filling gaps\n\n1. **`api.ts`** — everything else depends on it; 401 auto-logout and error-mapping behavior is currently unverified.\n2. **`transcript.ts`** — most complex branching logic in the file set, feeds the transcript UI directly, recently adjacent to a shipped bug fix (JIRA-AI-148).\n3. **`errors.ts`** — user-facing message correctness, easy to silently break during refactors.\n4. **`useCountUp`/`useToasts`** — pin down the leak behavior noted in the earlier performance audit so a fix can be verified against a regression test.\n5. **`formatting.ts`, `config.ts`, `cache.ts`, `useKeyboardShortcuts.ts`** — lower risk, but cheap to cover and guard against silent regressions.\n\nIntegration gap worth flagging: there's no test exercising the full `api.ts` → view flow (e.g., a component calling a real endpoint function and asserting on rendered error text via `friendlyApiError`). All current coverage is either pure-function unit tests or nonexistent — no MSW/fetch-mock integration layer exists in the test setup shown.\n",
